  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 44. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. コブラ — 首の周りを広げる種類が知られる毒蛇のなかま。\n2. 鼓膜 — 耳の中で音を受けて振動する薄い膜。\n3. コマーシャル — テレビなどで流す商品の広告。\n4. コミック — 漫画や漫画の本。\n5. 米粒 — 米の一つ一つの粒。\n6. コメディー — 見る人を笑わせる劇や映画など。\n7. コメント — 物事について述べる短い意見や説明。\n8. 小物 — 身の回りで使う小さな品物。\n9. 古文書 — 昔の人が書き残した手紙や記録などの文書。\n10. 子役 — 子どもの役を演じる俳優。\n11. コラム — 新聞などの短い意見や読み物の欄。\n12. コルク — 木の外側の皮から作る軽く弾力のある材料。\n13. コレクター — ある種類の物を集めることを楽しむ人。\n14. コロッケ — つぶしたいもなどに衣をつけて揚げた料理。\n15. 衣替え — 季節に合わせて着る衣類を入れ替えること。\n16. 声色 — 声の調子や響き。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
